       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the usual maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Usual maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and about 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day for extended-release. The largest single dose is typically 850\u20131,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This is double the maximum daily dose. That raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **500\u20131,000 mg PO two or three times daily**, or another dose\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
